From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:58:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a picture's own shape in screen-shaped tiles, and check
 it

- imageSizeMode "screen" for a grid tile: like "size", the picture takes
  the tile's shape (a TV game's capture at 4:3), but one turned the other
  way than the tile (an upright arcade game's capture in a landscape
  tile) takes the tile's shape turned, as tall as the tile and centred,
  instead of being stretched across it. The selected tile's video too.
  ImageComponent and VideoComponent: setKeepOrientation, applied when
  both sides of the size are set (ScreenShape::fit).
- A check for render tests, on with the environment variable
  ES_IMAGE_ASPECT: every image, video frame and slide drawn at another
  aspect ratio than the part of its texture it shows is logged once per
  element, source and size ("ImageAspect: ..."), so a test can fail on
  any stretch a theme did not mean.
- THEMES.md: imageSizeMode "screen".
